WHAT: Adds OLS test files documenting init-store-killed-by-overwrite patterns.
Tests confirm same-block dead store elimination already works, but cross-block
(loop-overwrite) patterns are not yet eliminated.

WHY: Documenting the gap before implementing the optimization. Tests serve as
regression tests and specify the expected behavior.

GAS IMPACT: None (test-only).

TEAM NOTES: These tests identify the [first; N] array init pattern as a target.
The same-block case is already handled; the loop-overwrite case (init 32 elements,
then overwrite in a for loop) is the one causing merkle's overhead.
